{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Moses spoke, and the priests the Levites.</b> He associated the priests with him to warn about diligence in the Torah, it being incumbent upon the priests to teach knowledge to the people, as it says: יוֹרוּ מִשְׁפָּטֶיךָ לְיַעֲקֹב (Deuteronomy 33:10)." "<b>Hasket.</b> Depict in your thought, as in אֵת סִכּוּת מַלְכְּכֶם (Amos 5:26)." "<b>And hear.</b> And reflect."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:19.588409798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}